text:
ashley: FYI I opened a docs PR to make function/tool outputs more tolerant: switch from a strict top-level \"output\" to a nullable \"result\" envelope. PR: https://git.redwood/infer/docs/pull/874

mike: quick ask  can you show the before/after example?

ashley: sure:
// before
{
  "tool": "price_lookup",
  "output": { "price": 9.99 }
}
// after
{
  "tool": "price_lookup",
  "result": { "payload": { "price": 9.99 }, "confidence": 0.86 }
}
// or when tool yields nothing:
{ "tool": "price_lookup", "result": null }

priya: SDK plan: add parseRelaxed() that tries strict JSON, a tiny pre-cleaner (trailing commas, stray tokens) and fallback to JSON5. will add unit tests for common broken outputs.

jordan: ill grep the examples repo and patch obvious `\"output\"` literals to `\"result.payload\"` with a // REVIEW comment for ambiguous cases. will open examples PR.

doc_bot: CI note: docs build queued. current run shows a few snapshot diffs where examples expect old shape. https://ci.redwood/infer/1280

mike: once jordan pushes examples patch ill run the smoke tests locally and in CI.

ashley: timeline: land schema + SDK helpers today, example patches tomorrow. small migration note in the Structured Outputs doc explaining null `result` and optional `reason` field requested. tag me on PRs. :thumbsup:
